  "body": "Main is red in `cargo test -p xtask` since the merge of PR #2904 (`bac4a96c7`, issue #917). Last green for these tests: `63200a698`. Found by the M5 main-health check on `3ffe2338f`.\n\nWhat happens: two gate-map tests fail.\n\n```\ngate_maps_tests::changed_box_fixture_selects_real_library_readers ... FAILED\ngate_maps_tests::changed_bspline_fixture_selects_real_library_readers ... FAILED\ntestdata/models/box.step: app library reader missing: [ ... geometry suites: step_metre_unit, step_twisted_flank, kernel suites ... ]\n```\n\n`assert_real_library_readers` (`xtask/src/gate_maps_tests.rs`) expects that a change to `testdata/models/box.step` (and the B-spline fixture) selects the `app suites: lib` and `ui suites: lib` steps. After #2904 the quick-tier plan for that file selects the geometry and kernel STEP suites, but no app or ui library step.\n\nProbable cause: #2904 moved the STEP reading out of the app and ui library code, so the scan no longer finds a library reader of these fixtures there. Either the test's expectation is now out of date, or the scan misses a reader that still exists. That is for the #917 owner to decide.\n\nDone means: `cargo test -p xtask` passes on main, and a change to a STEP fixture still selects every suite that reads it.\n",
